  "final_text": "Both objects exist. The rule is enabled.\n\n**Data findings (`kibana_sample_data_logs`)**\n- 14,074 requests from 1,001 distinct client IPs across 448 distinct URLs.\n- Timestamps run from 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03. That extends past today (2026-10-12), so the dashboard uses an absolute range of Oct 1 to Dec 31, 2026. A relative range like \"last 7 days\" would show mostly empty panels.\n- `response` only takes three values: 200 (12,832), 404 (801), and 503 (441). The only 5xx code is 503.\n- Top destination countries by `geo.dest` are CN, IN, and US.\n\n**Dashboard: \"EFF-f3d4102f Web logs overview\"**\n- ID: `eff-f3d4102f-web-logs-overview-5a7446c4673d`\n- URL: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-f3d4102f-web-logs-overview-5a7446c4673d\n- Five panels: Total requests (count), Unique client IPs (unique count of `clientip`), Requests over time (line by `@timestamp`), Responses by status code (pie by `response.keyword`), and Top destination countries (bar by `geo.dest`).\n\n**Alert rule: \"EFF-f3d4102f 5xx spike\"**\n- ID: `29c6b5b4-ffe5-439f-bf5b-81abe0c8e5ea`\n- Type `.es-query`, consumer `stackAlerts`, runs every 1m.\n- Fires when the count of documents matching `response.keyword` wildcard `5*` in the last 5 minutes is greater than 10.\n- Enabled. Status is \"pending\" until the first run.\n\n**Choices I made**\n- I matched 5xx with a wildcard on `response.keyword` because `response` is a string field.\n- I set the rule to enabled at creation rather than enabling it in a separate step.\n\n**Not verified**\n- The rule's stored query params. The read-back tool returns only the summary, and `KIBANA_TEST_API_KEY` isn't set in this shell, so I couldn't query the raw API.\n- Whether the rule will fire. The sample data is timestamped mostly in the future relative to now, so the sliding 5-minute window may often contain few or no 503s.",
